course: dictionary
lesson: 6465
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word nation has two. The first is a country, with its people, land and government. The second is a large group of people who share a history, language and culture, even when they do not have their own country.
explain: Context tells you which meaning is meant. «The United Nations» is a group of almost all countries working for peace, so nation means a country there. «First Nations in Canada» means Indigenous peoples, who share a history and culture, even though they are not their own country.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Ask: does the country meaning fit? If not, try the group-of-people meaning. The sentence will tell you which one works.
fact: A nation can mean a country, with its people, land and government.
fact: A nation can also mean a large group of people who share a history, language and culture.
fact: «First Nations» are Indigenous peoples of Canada, who were there long before European settlers arrived.
fact: «National» and «nationality» come from the same root word. «International» means between or across nations.
exercise: «In 1608 the French ... traded furs with First Nations by canoe.» In this sentence, who are First Nations? | French traders who sailed the seas | Beavers that lived in lakes | Foreign soldiers who built forts | *Indigenous peoples of Canada, with their own history and culture
exercise: «A copy hangs at the United Nations.» In this sentence, what does nation mean? | A group of people with a shared language only | A type of flag | *A country, with its people, land and government | A large city
exercise: Which meaning of nation fits «the whole nation watched»? | A map of the land | *The whole country's people | A small group of friends | A single family in one house
test: «Every new land already had people: First Nations, Inuit and Métis in Canada.» What does First Nations mean here? | *A group of people who share a history and culture | A government building | A set of rules for trade | A country with a flag and an anthem
test: Which word is related to nation and means across nations? | nationalise | notion | station | *international
exam: «Māori in New Zealand ... arrived around 1250 to 1300.» In this sentence, Māori are a nation in which sense? | A map of the islands | A country with its own government | A type of ship | *A group of people who share a history, language and culture
